1. Current reboot logic
This playbook reboots only if required.
The check uses:
needs-restarting -r

if available. If not available, it compares the running kernel with the latest installed kernel.
If you want to always reboot after patching, change this task:
- name: Reboot server if required
  ansible.builtin.reboot:
From:
when: patch_reboot_required == "YES"
To:
when: true
Also change this task:
- name: Mark reboot performed
From:
when: patch_reboot_required == "YES"
To:
when: true

